+[F1] [[thm-fd-smooth-periodic-incompressible-ivp]]: for smooth real divergence-free data and fixed $\nu\ge0$, the normalized periodic incompressible equation has a unique smooth local solution on an interval whose length depends on $d,s$, and the initial $H^s$ norm, but not on $\nu$ or higher norms. More precisely, for $M=\|u_0\|_{H^s}$ one may take $T_0=(2C_{d,s}\max\{1,M\})^{-1}$, and for every integer $m\ge s$ the quantitative Statement gives $\sup_{t\le T_0}\|u(t)\|_{H^m}\le\|u_0\|_{H^m}e^{2C_{d,m,s}MT_0}$ with constants independent of $\nu$.
 
 [F2] [[def-fd-polytropic-symmetric-variables]] and [[thm-fd-smooth-polytropic-euler-ivp]]: positive-density polytropic Euler is transformed to $q_t+\sum_jA_j(q)\partial_jq=0$, where each $A_j$ is a fixed linear symmetric-matrix map, and the local theorem supplies smooth positive-density solutions.
 
